Add /favicon.ico so the orange mark reaches Google search

Paul: "can you also change the logo on the website view. when it shows up on
Google search."

The root /favicon.ico was 404ing - it had never existed, only the PNG rel=icon
tags. Google checks that path first and some crawlers check only it. Written
as a multi-resolution ICO (16 to 256) from the new orange logo.png, and
declared in the head ahead of the PNGs.

No cache-buster on it, deliberately: Google re-crawls a favicon on its own
schedule and wants a stable URL. Browsers still get the busted PNGs.

The Organization schema logo in index.html already points at logo.png, so it
picked up the new mark with the file swap. Left bare of a query string on
purpose - structured data should name a canonical URL.

Regenerate favicon.ico whenever assets/brand/logo.png changes.
